# Class: obo:HP_0000005 (Mode of inheritance)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199>) obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HP_0000005 "The pattern in which a particular genetic trait or disorder is passed from one generation to the next.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId obo:HP_0000005 "HP:0001425")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId obo:HP_0000005 "HP:0001453")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId obo:HP_0000005 "HP:0001461")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId obo:HP_0000005 "HP:0010985")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:HP_0000005 "UMLS:C1708511")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:HP_0000005 "Inheritance")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:HP_0000005 "HP:0000005")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:HP_0000005 "While there is a close conceptual relationship between allelic requirement and inheritance, they serve different purposes; allelic requirement is necessary for variant annotation pipelines and to determine if a given variant in a specific context is relevant to the phenotype of the patient e.g. a heterozygous variant (in the absence of compound heterozygosity) is relevant for dominant but not for recessive disease; while inheritance is used for describing the mode of inheritance of a phenotype and is particularly applicable in the clinical setting for communicating recurrence risk, to guide family screening, and to guide reproductive advice.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HP_0000005 "Mode of inheritance")
SubClassOf(obo:HP_0000005 obo:PATO_0000001)

# Class: obo:HP_0000006 (Autosomal dominant inheritance)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199>) obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HP_0000006 "A mode of inheritance that is observed for traits related to a gene encoded on one of the autosomes (i.e., the human chromosomes 1-22) in which a trait manifests in heterozygotes. In the context of medical genetics, an autosomal dominant disorder is caused when a single copy of the mutant allele is present. Males and females are affected equally, and can both transmit the disorder with a risk of 50% for each child of inheriting the mutant allele.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId obo:HP_0000006 "HP:0001415")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId obo:HP_0000006 "HP:0001447")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId obo:HP_0000006 "HP:0001448")
