AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:HP_0000520 "Some sources define \"exophthalmos\" as a protrusion of the globe greater than 18 mm and \"proptosis\" as a protusion equal to or less than 18 mm. Others define \"exophthalmos\" as protusion secondary to endocrine dysfunction and \"proptosis\" as any non-endocrine-mediated protusion (Source: Wikipedia). This finding should be distinguished frm underdevelopment of the supraorbital ridge or maxilla/zygoma. In proptosis, the globe is anteriorly protuberant to the overall plane of the face.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HP_0000520 "Proptosis")
