# Class: obo:HP_0002072 (Chorea)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:20589866") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HP_0002072 "Chorea (Greek for 'dance') refers to widespread arrhythmic involuntary movements of a forcible, jerky and restless fashion. It is a random-appearing sequence of one or more discrete involuntary movements or movement fragments. Movements appear random because of variability in timing, duration or location. Each movement may have a distinct start and end. However, movements may be strung together and thus may appear to flow randomly from one muscle group to another. Chorea can involve the trunk, neck, face, tongue, and extremities.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId obo:HP_0002072 "HP:0002397")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:HP_0002072 "SNOMEDCT_US:271700006")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:HP_0002072 "UMLS:C0008489")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:HP_0002072 "UMLS:C4020858")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:HP_0002072 "Choreic movements")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:HP_0002072 "Choreiform movements")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:HP_0002072 "Choreatic disease")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:HP_0002072 "HP:0002072")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HP_0002072 "Chorea")
SubClassOf(obo:HP_0002072 obo:HP_0004305)

