# Class: obo:HP_0003401 (Assessment of pinch strengh using B & L gauge)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199>) obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HP_0003401 "Abnormal sensations such as tingling, pricking, or numbness of the skin with no apparent physical cause.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:source "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PROMOT_0100008") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HP_0003401 "An evaluation procedure that uses a B&L gauge to assess pinch strengh. The test measuring the force of the lateral clamps, between the thumb and the index finger, allows quantifying the maximum voluntary strength of the hand and forearm muscles during a pinching action. This is an indicator of the level of hand function.")
