# Class: obo:HP_0003470 (Paralysis)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199>) obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HP_0003470 "Paralysis of voluntary muscles means loss of contraction due to interruption of one or more motor pathways from the brain to the muscle fibers. Although the word paralysis is often used interchangeably to mean either complete or partial loss of muscle strength, it is preferable to use paralysis or plegia for complete or severe loss of muscle strength, and paresis for partial or slight loss. Motor paralysis results from deficits of the upper motor neurons (corticospinal, corticobulbar, or subcorticospinal). Motor paralysis is often accompanied by an impairment in the facility of movement.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:HP_0003470 "SNOMEDCT_US:44695005")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:HP_0003470 "UMLS:C0522224")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType hp:layperson) oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:HP_0003470 "Inability to move")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType hp:layperson) oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:HP_0003470 "Paralysis")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:HP_0003470 "HP:0003470")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HP_0003470 "Paralysis")
SubClassOf(obo:HP_0003470 obo:HP_0011442)

# Class: obo:HP_0003473 (Fatigable weakness)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199>) obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HP_0003473 "A type of weakness that occurs after a muscle group is used and lessens if the muscle group has some rest. That is, there is diminution of strength with repetitive muscle actions.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId obo:HP_0003473 "HP:0003399")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId obo:HP_0003473 "HP:0003428")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId obo:HP_0003473 "HP:0100794")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:HP_0003473 "UMLS:C0947912")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:HP_0003473 "Fatigable weakness of limb muscles")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType hp:uk_spelling) oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:HP_0003473 "Generalised muscle weakness due to defect at the neuromuscular junction")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:HP_0003473 "Generalized muscle weakness due to defect at the neuromuscular junction")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:HP_0003473 "Myasthenia")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:HP_0003473 "Myasthenic weakness")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:HP_0003473 "Proximal muscle weakness due to defect at the neuromuscular junction")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:HP_0003473 "HP:0003473")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:HP_0003473 "This type of weakness is pathognomonic for an abnormality of the neuromuscular junction such as myasthenia gravis. A characteristic form of muscular weakness that worsens after use of affected muscles. Myasthenia is caused by failure of neuromuscular transmission, which results from the binding of autoantibodies to proteins involved in signaling at the neuromuscular junction, including especially the nicotinic acetyl choline receptor (AChR) or, less frequently, a muscle-specific tyrosine kinase involved in AChR clustering.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HP_0003473 "Fatigable weakness")
SubClassOf(obo:HP_0003473 obo:HP_0001324)
SubClassOf(obo:HP_0003473 obo:HP_0012638)

