# Class: obo:HP_0025031 (Abnormality of the digestive system)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:HP_0025031 "Any anomaly of the digestive system, a collection of organs that is made up of the gastrointestinal tract and the liver, pancreas, and gallbladder. The gastrointestinal tract is a series of hollow organs joined in a long, twisting tube from the mouth to the anus, including the mouth, esophagus, stomach, small intestine, large intestine and anus.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HP_0025031 "Abnormality of the digestive system")
SubClassOf(obo:HP_0025031 obo:HP_0000118)

# Class: obo:HP_0025032 (Abnormality of digestive system physiology)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HP_0025032 "A functional anomaly of the digestive system.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HP_0025032 "Abnormality of digestive system physiology")
SubClassOf(obo:HP_0025032 obo:HP_0025031)

# Class: obo:HP_0025085 (Bloody diarrhea)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HP_0025085 "Passage of many stools containing blood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType hp:layperson) oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:HP_0025085 "Blood in stool")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType hp:layperson) oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:HP_0025085 "Bloody stool")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType hp:layperson) oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:HP_0025085 "Bloody bowel movement")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType hp:layperson) oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:HP_0025085 "Bloody diarrhea")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:HP_0025085 "Diarrhea that contains bright red or maroon-colored blood may be referred to as hematochezia, while melena is used to describe black, tarry, and smelly diarrhea.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HP_0025085 "Bloody diarrhea")
SubClassOf(obo:HP_0025085 obo:HP_0011458)

# Class: obo:HP_0025142 (Constitutional symptom)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HP_0025142 "A symptom or manifestation indicating a systemic or general effect of a disease and that may affect the general well-being or status of an individual.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:HP_0025142 "Note that we use the preferred term label constitutional symptom because this reflects common usage, but we do not restrict the term or its descendents to the narrow meaning of symptom, i.e., a complaint related by a patient to a physician. There is no generally accepted classification of what defines a constitutional symptom, but examples include weight loss, fatigue, general weakness, night sweats, shaking, chills, fever, and vomiting.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HP_0025142 "Constitutional symptom")
SubClassOf(obo:HP_0025142 obo:HP_0000118)

# Class: obo:HP_0025153 (Transient)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HP_0025153 "Short-lived and not permanent. This term applies to a phenotypic abnormality that is temporary and of short duration.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HP_0025153 "Transient")
SubClassOf(obo:HP_0025153 obo:HP_0031797)

