AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HP_0032180 "Abnormal circulating metabolite concentration")
SubClassOf(obo:HP_0032180 obo:HP_0001939)

# Class: obo:HP_0033127 (Abnormality of the musculoskeletal system)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HP_0033127 "An anomaly of the musculoskeletal system, which consists of the bones of the skeleton, muscles, cartilage, tendons, ligaments, joints, and other connective tissue. The musculoskeletal system supports the weight of the body, maintains body position and produces movements of the body or of parts of the body.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HP_0033127 "Abnormality of the musculoskeletal system")
SubClassOf(obo:HP_0033127 obo:HP_0000118)

# Class: obo:HP_0033354 (Abnormal urine metabolite level)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HP_0033354 "Any deviation from the normal amount of a metabolite in urine.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:HP_0033354 "As water reabsorption in kidneys affect urinary solute concentrations, various methods are applied to normalize the measured concentration. Frequently, concentrations are reported as a ratio to urinary creatinine. The HPO terms in this subhierarchy therefore use the word 'level' to indicate that appropriate normalization has been performed before concluding that the amount of the indicated metabolite is abnormal.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HP_0033354 "Abnormal urine metabolite level")
SubClassOf(obo:HP_0033354 obo:HP_0000119)
SubClassOf(obo:HP_0033354 obo:HP_0001939)

# Class: obo:HP_0034345 (Mendelian inheritance)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HP_0034345 "A mode of inheritance of diseases whose pathophysiology can be traced back to deleterious variants in a single gene. The inheritance patterns of these single-gene (monogenic) diseases are often referred to as Mendelian in honor of Gregor Mendel.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:HP_0034345 "Mendelian, or monogenic, inheritance of human diseases refers to patterns of transmission of recognizable disease entities. In many cases variability of clinical manifestations is observed and may be related to variation in other genes, environmental factors, or other unknown causes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HP_0034345 "Mendelian inheritance")
SubClassOf(obo:HP_0034345 obo:HP_0000005)

