# Class: obo:MONDO_0006955 (rheumatic heart disease)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "NCIT:C34882") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0006955 "An autoinflammatory condition following an infection with Group A Beta Hemolytic Streptococcus (GABHS), in which the heart is attacked by antibodies formed in reaction to a recent GABHS infection. Chief anatomic changes of the valve include leaflet thickening, commissural fusion, and shortening and thickening of the tendinous cords, all of which can result in valvular dysfunction.")
