# Class: obo:MONDO_0009711 (congenital fiber-type disproportion myopathy)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "NCIT:C120046") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:31578728") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0009711 "A rare genetic disorder caused by mutations in the TPM3, ACTA1, RYR1 or SEPN1 genes. It is inherited in an autosomal dominant or recessive pattern and rarely in an X-linked pattern. It manifests with myopathy throughout the body, particularly in the muscles of the shoulders, upper arms, hips, and thighs. Affected individuals may have contractures, lordosis, or scoliosis. In a minority of cases mild to severe breathing problems may occur.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:source "MONDO:equivalentTo") oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:MONDO_0009711 "DOID:0080102")
