# Class: obo:MONDO_0010161 (tyrosinemia type I)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Orphanet:882") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0010161 "Tyrosinemia type 1 (HTI) is an inborn error of tyrosine catabolism caused by defective activity of fumarylacetoacetate hydrolase (FAH) and is characterized by progressive liver disease, renal tubular dysfunction, porphyria-like crises and a dramatic improvement in prognosis following treatment with nitisinone.")
