# Class: obo:MONDO_0010949 (Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 2B)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Orphanet:99936") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0010949 "Autosomal dominant Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 2B (CMT2B) is a severe form of axonal Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease, a peripheral sensorimotor neuropathy. CMT2B onset, in the 2nd or 3rd decade, is characterized by ulcerations and infections of feet. Symmetric and distal weakness develops mostly in the legs together with a severe symmetric distal sensory loss, tendon reflexes are only reduced at ankles and foot deformities, including pes cavus or planus and hammer toes, appear in childhood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:source "MONDO:equivalentTo") oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:MONDO_0010949 "DOID:0110159")
