# Class: obo:MONDO_0011408 (hereditary spastic paraplegia 10)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Orphanet:100991") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0011408 "Autosomal dominant spastic paraplegia type 10 (SPG10) is a rare type of hereditary spastic paraplegia that can present as either a pure form of spastic paraplegia with lower limb spasticity, hyperreflexia and extensor plantar responses, presenting in childhood or adolescence, or as a complex phenotype associated with additional manifestations including peripheral neuropathy with upper limb amyotrophy, moderate intellectual disability and parkinsonism. Deafness and retinitis pigmentosa were reported in one case.")
