# Class: obo:MONDO_0012096 (Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease axonal type 2L)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Orphanet:99945") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0012096 "Autosomal dominant Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 2L (CMT2L) is a form of axonal Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease, a peripheral sensorimotor neuropathy. In the single family reported to date, CMT2L onset is between 15 and 33 years. Patients present with a symmetric distal weakness of legs and occasionally of the hands, absent or reduced tendon reflexes, distal legs sensory loss and frequently a pes cavus. Progression is slow.")
