AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Orphanet:217371") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0013111 "Acute infantile liver failure due to mtDNA-encoded proteins synthesis defect is a very rare mitochondrial respiratory chain deficiency described in fewer than 10 infants, primarily of middle Eastern descent, and characterized clinically by transient but life-threatening liver failure with elevated liver enzymes, jaundice, vomiting, coagulopathy, hyperbilirubinemia, and lactic acidemia.")
