# Class: obo:MONDO_0015240 (digitotalar dysmorphism)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Orphanet:1146") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0015240 "Digitotalar dysmorphism, also known as distal arthrogryposis type 1 (DA1), is an autosomal dominant congenital anomaly characterized by contractures of the distal regions of the hands and feet with no facial involvement or any additional anomalies. It is the most common type of distal arthrogryposis.")
