# Class: obo:MONDO_0015454 (multiple carboxylase deficiency)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Orphanet:148") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0015454 "Multiple carboxylase deficiency (MCD) is a term used to describe inborn errors of biotin metabolism characterized by reduced activities of biotin-dependent enzymes resulting in a wide spectrum of symptoms, including feeding difficulty, breathing difficulties, lethargy, seizures, skin rash, alopecia, and developmental delay.")
