AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Orphanet:26") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0016826 "An inborn error of vitamin B12 (cobalamin) metabolism characterized by megaloblastic anemia, lethargy, failure to thrive, developmental delay, intellectual deficit and seizures. There are four complementation classes of cobalamin defects (cblC, cblD, cblF and cblJ) that are responsible for methylmalonic acidemia - homocystinuria (methylmalonic acidemia - homocystinuria cblC, cblD cblF and cblJ).")
