# Class: obo:MONDO_0017276 (frontotemporal dementia)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Orphanet:282") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0017276 "Frontotemporal dementia (FTD) comprises a group of neurodegenerative disorders, characterized by progressive changes in behavior, executive dysfunction and language impairment, as a result of degeneration of the medial prefrontal and frontoinsular cortices. Four clinical subtypes have been identified: semantic dementia, progressive non-fluent aphasia, behavioral variant FTD and right temporal lobar atrophy.")
