# Class: obo:MONDO_0018011 (juvenile overlap myositis)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Orphanet:329894") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0018011 "Juvenile overlap myositis is a rare juvenile idiopathic inflammatory myopathy characterized by the association of inflammatory myositis (manifesting with acral erythema, progressive weakness of the limbs, pain, general fatigue, moodiness or crankiness) with clinical and/or laboratory features of other autoimmune diseases (e.g. systemic lupus erythematosus, localized scleroderma, diabetes). Cardiac involvement has been reported in some patients.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:source "MONDO:GARD") oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:MONDO_0018011 "GARD:0021497")
