AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Orphanet:352723") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0018133 "Attenuated Chédiak-Higashi syndrome (CHS) is a very rare and atypical form of CHS, a genetic disorder characterized by partial oculocutaneous albinism (OCA), severe immunodeficiency, mild bleeding, neurological dysfunction and lymphoproliferative disorder.")
