# Class: obo:MONDO_0018908 (non-Hodgkin lymphoma)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "NCIT:C3211") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0018908 "Distinct from Hodgkin lymphoma both morphologically and biologically, non-Hodgkin lymphoma (NHL) is characterized by the absence of Reed-Sternberg cells, can occur at any age, and usually presents as a localized or generalized lymphadenopathy associated with fever and weight loss. The clinical course varies according to the morphologic type. NHL is clinically classified as indolent, aggressive, or having a variable clinical course. NHL can be of B-or T-/NK-cell lineage.")
