# Class: obo:MONDO_0018959 (potassium-aggravated myotonia)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Orphanet:612") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0018959 "Potassium-aggravated myotonia (PAM) is a muscular channelopathy presenting with a pure myotonia dramatically aggravated by potassium ingestion, with variable cold sensitivity and no episodic weakness. This group includes three forms: myotonia fluctuans, myotonia permanens, and acetazolamide-responsive myotonia.")
