# Class: obo:MONDO_0019065 (amyloidosis)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "NCIT:C2868") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0019065 "A disorder characterized by the localized or diffuse accumulation of amyloid protein in various anatomic sites. It may be primary, due to clonal plasma cell proliferations; secondary, due to long standing infections, chronic inflammatory disorders, or malignancies; or familial. It may affect the nerves, skin, tongue, joints, heart, liver, spleen, kidneys and adrenal glands.")
