# Class: obo:MONDO_0020478 (Leber plus disease)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Orphanet:99718") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MONDO_0020478 "Leber `plus' disease describes patients with the clinical features of Leber's hereditary optic neuropathy (LHON) in combination with other serious systemic or neurological abnormalities. These abnormalities include: postural tremor, motor disorder, multiple sclerosis-like syndrome, spinal cord disease, skeletal changes, Parkinsonism with dystonia, anarthria, dystonia, motor and sensory peripheral neuropathy, spasticity and mild encephalopathy. It is caused by maternally-inherited mitochondrial DNA (mtDNA) mutations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:source "MONDO:equivalentTo") oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:MONDO_0020478 "DOID:0111754")
