# Class: obo:UBERON_0000107 (cleavage stage)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "GO:0040016") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Wikipedia:Cleavage_(embryo)") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:UBERON_0000107 "The first few specialized divisions of an activated animal egg; Stage consisting of division of cells in the early embryo. The zygotes of many species undergo rapid cell cycles with no significant growth, producing a cluster of cells the same size as the original zygote. The different cells derived from cleavage are called blastomeres and form a compact mass called the morula. Cleavage ends with the formation of the blastula.")
