# Class: obo:UBERON_0000307 (blastula)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Wikipedia:Blastula") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:UBERON_0000307 "Organism at the blastula stage - an early stage of embryonic development in animals. It is produced by cleavage of a fertilized ovum and consists of a spherical layer of around 128 cells surrounding a central fluid-filled cavity called the blastocoel. The blastula follows the morula and precedes the gastrula in the developmental sequence.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000116 obo:UBERON_0000307 "TODO - check relationship with epiblast. Note in FMA this is not a subclass of embryo, but in uberon embryo is the whole organism from zygote onwards and thus includes the blastula")
