AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:UBERON_0005721 "the intermediate mesoderm of the chick embryo acquires its ability to form kidneys through its interactions with the paraxial mesoderm [ISBN:9780878932504 \"Developmental Biology\", PMID:10720431 \"Signals from trunk paraxial mesoderm induce pronephros formation in chick intermediate mesoderm\"]. These interactions induce the expression of TFs including Lim1, Pax2 and Pax6 that cause the intermediate mesoderm to form the kidney")
