# Class: <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/100> (Ubiquitin like modifier activating enzymes)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:description <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/100> "Ubiquitin-activating enzymes, also known as E1 enzymes, catalyze the first step in the ubiquitination reaction, which (among other things) can target a protein for degradation via a proteasome. This covalent attachment of ubiquitin or ubiquitin-like proteins to targeted proteins is a major mechanism for regulating protein function in eukaryotic organisms.")
