# Class: <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1253> (Scavenger receptors)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:description <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1253> "Scavenger receptors are a group of receptors that recognize modified low-density lipoprotein (LDL) by oxidation or acetylation. This naming is based on a function of cleaning (scavenging): Scavenger receptors widely recognize and take up macromolecules that have a negative charge, like modified LDL.")
