AnnotationAssertion(terms:description <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1428> "This family consists of the G protein alpha subunit group I (inhibitory), which includes G alpha-I, G alpha-O, G alpha-T and G alpha-Z. G alpha-I proteins were originally identified by their receptor-mediated inhibition of the cAMP-generating enzyme adenylyl cyclase.")
