# Class: <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/2293> (Proteins encoded by multiple genes)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:description <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/2293> "This group lists protein coding genes that encode a protein that is identical to that encoded by another gene or genes. The list was constructed from a set of UniProt accessions that are associated with multiple genes. The list is limited to genes on the current reference assembly and excludes proteins encoded by read-through transcripts. Genes that encode the same protein share root symbols. Note the H3C root is associated with two different proteins - one encoded by a cluster of genes on 6p22.1 and the other by a cluster of three genes on 1q21.2 (H3C13-15).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/2293> "Proteins encoded by multiple genes")
SubClassOf(<https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/2293> obo:SO_0005855)

