# Class: <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3517> (Transaminases)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:description <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3517> "Transaminases (or Aminotransferases) (Enzyme Commission [EC] 2.6.1.-) are pyridoxal 5′-phosphate–dependent enzymes that catalyze the transamination reactions between amino acid donor and keto acid acceptor substrates.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3517> "Aminotransferases")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3517> "Transaminases")
SubClassOf(<https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3517> obo:SO_0005855)

# Class: <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3533> (Choline kinase family)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:description <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3533> "Choline kinases catalyse the conversion of choline to phosphocholine, which is further converted to cytidine diphosphate-coline (CDP-choline) in the biosynthesis of phosphatidylcholine (PC). PC is a major constituent of the phospholipid bilayer which constitutes the eukaryotic cell membrane, and regulates cell signal transduction. Functional choline kinase exists as a dimer, and can form homodimers or heterodimers with differential dynamics dependent on the tissue type. CHKA homodimers display higher enzymatic activity than CHKB homodimers and CHKA/B heterodimers with tissues differing in their relative expression of the varying isoforms.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3533> "CHK")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3533> "Choline kinase family")
SubClassOf(<https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3533> obo:SO_0005855)

# Class: <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3556> (Phosphofructokinase family)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:description <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3556> "Phosphofructokinase (PFK) catalyses the phosphorylation of fructose 6-phosphate (F6P) to fructose 1,6-bisphosphate (F1,6BP) and plays a central role in the glycolytic pathway. The human enzymes are encoded by 3 paralogous genes: PFKM, PFKL and PFKP. While the isoforms were named for the tissue that they are prevalent or originally found (muscle, liver and platelet respectively) they are not limited to these tissues. The functional enzyme is a tetramer and can be formed from one or more isoforms. The kinetic/regulatory properties vary with subunit composition.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3556> "6-phosphofructo-1-kinase subunits")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3556> "PFK")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3556> "Phosphofructokinase family")
SubClassOf(<https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3556> obo:SO_0005855)

