# Class: <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/437> (Glycogen phosphorylases)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:description <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/437> "Glycogen phosphorylase is one of the phosphorylase enzymes ( EC 2.4.1.1 ). Glycogen phosphorylase catalyzes the rate-limiting step in glycogenolysis in animals by releasing glucose-1-phosphate from the terminal alpha-1,4-glycosidic bond. Glycogen phosphorylase is also studied as a model protein regulated by both reversible phosphorylation and allosteric effects.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/437> "PYG")
