# Class: <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/777> (Tropomyosins)

AnnotationAssertion(terms:description <https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/777> "Tropomyosins are a large family of integral components of actin filaments that play a critical role in regulating the function of actin filaments in both muscle and nonmuscle cells. These proteins consist of rod-shaped coiled-coil hetero- or homo-dimers that lie along the α-helical groove of most actin filaments. Interaction occurs along the length of the actin filament, with dimers aligning in a head-to-tail fashion.")
